.env.*.local
# issue #126 verification finding 9: a negation here USED to un-ignore
# apps/cloud/supabase/.env — the exact canonical path Supabase's own docs
# tell you to put SECRETS in for config.toml's env(...) substitutions (see
# `openai_api_key = "env(OPENAI_API_KEY)"` etc. in config.toml). Today's
# content there is non-secret (two localhost URLs), but leaving that path
# permanently un-ignored means the next person who follows Supabase's docs
# and adds a real secret to it commits that secret with no warning. Fixed
# (issue #12's original need — committed local-dev defaults for
# config.toml's env(SUPABASE_SITE_URL)/env(SUPABASE_ADDITIONAL_REDIRECT_URL))
# by committing apps/cloud/supabase/.env.example instead (see its header) and
# leaving supabase/.env itself covered by the blanket `.env` rule above, same
# as every other real secrets file in this repo.

